00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.490
However, this may be
different in future versions.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.730
For now, it suffices to say
that development on Cloud Tasks

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.320
has froze for Python 2.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.840
Hence why the client
library is on version 1,

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.690
whereas Python 3's
is on version 2.

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:21.120
Finally, we know
from modules 2 and 3

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:24.285
that Cloud NDB is just a
migration tool for Python 2 App

00:01:24.285 --> 00:01:25.320
Engine developers.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:28.710
From modules 6 and 10, we
know that Cloud Firestore

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:31.920
is the latest NoSQL database
solution from Google Cloud.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.340
By going straight there, we
get to jump over the Cloud

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:36.450
Datastore migration.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.100
Moving directly
to Firestore does

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.080
require a completely
different project,

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.270
so this endeavor is
